    <string name="automation_apps">Apps allowed to be read</string>
    <string name="automation_service_description">OMyMoney reads visible transaction pages in your selected apps while the device is unlocked. When payment has succeeded and the amount is clear, the transaction is saved automatically to the current book and a confirmation is shown. If the page has no time, the recognition time is used and marked as estimated. If the paying account is unclear, it stays unidentified and no balance is deducted from cash or other accounts. If you separately grant system notification access, OMyMoney reads transaction notifications from selected apps. All notification results remain pending review and are not recorded automatically; notification times are never treated as transaction times. OMyMoney does not click or pay automatically, and does not read passwords, editable input fields or nodes marked as sensitive by the system. With separate consent for diagnostic logging, it records relevant app events, readable pages and suspected transaction notification samples from all supported apps, including formats not yet recognized. These logs are uploaded after you pair a server. You can stop automatic bookkeeping, diagnostic logging and uploads, or separately revoke accessibility and notification access in system settings. Manual entry is unaffected.</string>
